---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/marketing-layout.astro';
import AtollIllustration from '../components/marketing/AtollIllustration.astro';
import ThaanaIllustration from '../components/marketing/ThaanaIllustration.astro';
import { Button } from '@veli-design/react/button';
import '../styles/design.css';
const a = '/images/marketing/';
const forces = [
  {
    name: 'reef',
    title: 'Reef',
    icon: '9709d.svg',
    description: 'Light gives the interface depth, guiding the eye to what matters first.',
  },
  {
    name: 'ocean',
    title: 'Ocean',
    icon: '8011b.svg',
    description: 'Texture adds quiet tactility, the way sand grains catch the sun.',
  },
  {
    name: 'wind',
    title: 'Wind',
    icon: '87dbe.svg',
    description: 'Motion carries people forward, like water moving around an island.',
  },
];
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Designing Veli | Veli Design System"
  description="How the sand of the Maldives shaped a design system for government services."
  variant="design"
>
  <div class="design-page">
    <canvas class="design-hero-field" data-design-field="hero" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <section class="design-hero" aria-labelledby="design-title">
      <h1 id="design-title">Designing Veli</h1><p>
        How the sand of the Maldives shaped a design system for government services
      </p>
    </section>
    <div class="design-container">
      <section class="design-section design-shared" aria-labelledby="shared-ground">
        <div class="design-section-heading">
          <div>
            <img src={`${a}bc7ff.svg`} width="46" height="5" alt="" /><h2 id="shared-ground">
              Built on shared<br />ground
            </h2>
          </div><p>
            People come to government online to get something done. Too often, every service looks
            different, works differently, and has to be learned from scratch. Every digital service
            has its own purpose and audience. But they don’t need their own foundation.
          </p>
        </div>
        <figure class="design-one-system" data-design-one-system>
          <figcaption>One system</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>
      <p class="design-reflection">
        The challenge wasn't designing another set of screens. It was creating something teams
        across every ministry could build on without losing their own purpose. Before choosing a
        single colour or component, we had to decide what kind of system this should be, and what it
        should be made of.
      </p>
      <p class="design-interlude">Sand doesn't exist in isolation.</p>
      <section class="design-section design-forces" aria-labelledby="patient-forces">
        <div class="design-section-heading">
          <div>
            <img src={`${a}5f051.svg`} width="46" height="5" alt="" /><h2 id="patient-forces">
              Shaped by<br />patient forces
            </h2>
          </div><p>
            People come to government online to get something done. Too often, every service looks
            different, works differently, and has to be learned from scratch. Every digital service
            has its own purpose and audience. But they don’t need their own foundation.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="design-force-grid">
          {
            forces.map((force) => (
              <article
                class="design-force-card"
                data-design-field={force.name}
                data-design-preview-host
              >
                <>
                  <canvas aria-hidden="true" />
                  <div
                    class="design-preview-animation design-preview-force"
                    data-design-animation={force.name}
                    aria-hidden="true"
                  />
                  <div class="design-force-icon">
                    <img src={`${a}${force.icon}`} width="100" height="100" alt="" />
                  </div>
                  <h3>{force.title}</h3>
                  <p>{force.description}</p>
                </>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
        <div class="design-responds">
          <p>A design system responds to</p><ul>
            <li>Human behaviour</li><li>Accessibility</li><li>Technology</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="design-section design-layers" aria-labelledby="sand-to-atoll">
        <div class="design-section-heading">
          <div>
            <img src={`${a}5f051.svg`} width="46" height="5" alt="" /><h2 id="sand-to-atoll">
              From sand to<br />atoll
            </h2>
          </div><p>
            Veli is built in layers, the same way the islands are. To form one unified nation. Veli
            is built in layers, the same way the islands are. To form one unified nation.
          </p>
        </div>
        <figure class="design-atoll" data-design-preview-host>
          <div class="design-atoll-canvas"><AtollIllustration /></div><figcaption class="sr-only">
            Veli foundations grow into coral components, reef patterns, island blocks, and atolls of
            services.
          </figcaption>
          <div class="design-preview-animation" data-design-animation="atoll" aria-hidden="true">
          </div>
        </figure>
        <p class="design-atoll-key" aria-hidden="true">
          Foundations → Components → Patterns → Blocks → Services
        </p>
      </section>
      <section class="design-crystalline" aria-labelledby="crystalline">
        <img class="design-section-dots" src={`${a}5f051.svg`} width="46" height="5" alt="" /><h2
          id="crystalline"
        >
          Crystalline Sand<br />philosophy
        </h2><p>
          The Crystalline Sand philosophy dictates how light, texture and motion function across
          government networks.
        </p><div class="design-crystalline-grid">
          <div class="design-light-art" data-design-scene="light" data-design-preview-host>
            <img
              src={`${a}444e0.svg`}
              width="338"
              height="301"
              alt="Light: soft blue, teal, and white illumination"
            />
            <div class="design-preview-animation" data-design-animation="light" aria-hidden="true">
            </div>
          </div><div data-design-scene="texture" data-design-preview-host>
            <img
              src={`${a}2894e.svg`}
              width="385"
              height="404"
              alt="Texture: grains of sand flowing through a field"
            />
            <div
              class="design-preview-animation"
              data-design-animation="texture"
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
            </div>
          </div><div data-design-scene="curve" data-design-preview-host>
            <img
              src={`${a}c7c33.svg`}
              width="386"
              height="404"
              alt="Motion: a smooth curve with measured control points"
            />
            <div class="design-preview-animation" data-design-animation="curve" aria-hidden="true">
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="design-section design-movement" aria-labelledby="purposeful-motion">
        <div class="design-section-heading">
          <div>
            <img src={`${a}5f051.svg`} width="46" height="5" alt="" /><h2 id="purposeful-motion">
              Movement with<br />purpose
            </h2>
          </div><p>
            Motion gives digital experiences a sense of direction. In Veli, every movement has a
            purpose — guided by clarity and natural transitions. Motion gives digital experiences a
            sense of direction. In Veli, every movement has a purpose — guided by clarity and
            natural transitions.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="design-motion-demo" data-design-scene="motion">
          <div class="design-motion-native">
            <img
              class="design-motion-backdrop"
              src={`${a}33ffa.svg`}
              width="1665"
              height="684"
              alt=""
            /><div class="design-guide" aria-hidden="true" data-design-preview-host>
              {[0, 1, 2, 3].map((i) => <span style={{ '--i': i }} />)}
              <div class="design-preview-animation" data-design-animation="guide"></div>
            </div><div class="design-connect" aria-hidden="true" data-design-preview-host>
              <img src={`${a}12e9b.svg`} width="64" height="64" alt="" /><img
                src={`${a}d02dc.svg`}
                width="64"
                height="64"
                alt=""
              /><img src={`${a}f8b0a.svg`} width="64" height="64" alt="" />
              <div class="design-preview-animation" data-design-animation="connect"></div>
            </div><div class="design-ripple" aria-hidden="true" data-design-preview-host>
              <img src={`${a}b4bb8.svg`} width="382" height="260" alt="" />
              <div class="design-preview-animation" data-design-animation="respond"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="design-motion-captions">
          <div>
            <h3>Guide</h3><p>
              Like water moving around an island, transitions guide people through an experience.
            </p>
          </div><div>
            <h3>Connect</h3><p>
              Like sand shifting with the tide, interfaces respond to people’s actions.
            </p>
          </div><div>
            <h3>Respond</h3><p>
              Like a ripple on still water, every action gets an immediate answer.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="design-section design-rooted" aria-labelledby="rooted-thaana">
        <div class="design-section-heading">
          <div>
            <img src={`${a}5f051.svg`} width="46" height="5" alt="" /><h2 id="rooted-thaana">
              Rooted in<br />Thaana
            </h2>
          </div><p>
            Language is part of accessibility. A service that only works well in English leaves out
            many of the people it’s meant to serve, including the many citizens who are more
            comfortable reading Dhivehi. In Veli, Dhivehi is a first language of the system, so
            everyone can use government services in the language they know best.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="design-thaana" data-design-scene="thaana" data-design-preview-host>
          <p class="sr-only" id="thaana-preview-instructions">
            Use arrow keys to explore the letters. Press Enter or Space, or tap a letter, to pin or
            release its green bloom.
          </p>
          <div class="design-thaana-art" lang="dv" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="design-thaana-native">
              <ThaanaIllustration /><div
                class="design-preview-animation"
                data-design-animation="thaana"
              >
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="design-thaana-meta">
            <p>Dhivehi typefaces<br />Veli Design System<br />Script No. 001</p><p>
              Regular — MV Faseyha<br />Medium — MV A Waheed<br />Bold — MV Aaamu FK
            </p><p>Thaana · written right to left<br />24 letters · 11 fili</p><p>
              Thaana<br /><span lang="dv" dir="rtl">ތާނަ</span>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="design-closing">
        <div>
          <p>
            A shared language between government teams, designers, developers and the citizens they
            serve — unified, calm, and recognisably Maldivian.
          </p><Button
            as="a"
            href="https://www.figma.com/design/tW1kYAZ4r80k2EUadpotTa/Design-System-Doc-Site"
            intent="accent"
            size="xl">Explore in Figma</Button
          >
        </div><canvas data-design-field="closing" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</MarketingLayout>
<script>
  import { initDesignMotion } from '../scripts/design-motion';
  initDesignMotion();
</script>
